# Stage 3 — SAME ID, now `ready`: it verifies its parent, verification mode is
# executable, and (test-side, not here) a specTest anchor binds the executable
# half — which makes it an ENABLED VERIFIER, so the parent earns `has-verifier`.
# From here, `sdp build` emits the step contract in 4-seam/contracts/.
#
# Note what is NOT in this file: no step bindings, no test code, no delivery
# facts. Intent and implementation stay split (JS-B1.4); facts are derived.

spec orders.create-order.valid-cart
  example · story · ready
  refines  orders.create-order
  verifies orders.create-order

Valid cart creates an order

  The happy path of create-order: a fully stocked cart becomes an order and
  the order math holds.

  Given a customer has a cart with one or more line items
    And every cart item is in stock
    And each line item has a positive quantity and a unit price
  When the customer submits the cart for order creation
  Then an order is created
    And the order total equals the sum of quantity times unit price per line
    And the order contains the original cart lines

  verification executable
    The order result contains a stable id.
    The returned total matches the cart math.
